    "sha": "ac58a3258455e2485def5d936530e641f8168690",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGFjNThhMzI1ODQ1NWUyNDg1ZGVmNWQ5MzY1MzBlNjQxZjgxNjg2OTA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T07:07:42Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T07:07:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): flip the flat cap facets of a refined STEP face\n\nThe #2600 split holds a curved face's facet edges to its surface. It\nmeasures edges only, so it left flat \"cap\" facets on the wall of\nbar_cross_holes.step: three points on the cylinder, the apex over the\nmiddle of the long edge. Their normals stood up to 65 degrees off the\nradius (2 147 of 131 834 wall facets over 25 degrees). The feature graph\nread their edges as creases on the smooth wall: 3 701 pickable edges, and\n116 tangent pieces that feature_edge_g1_join refused. Main was red.\n\nA refined face now gets Lawson's edge flip, measured in space: an inside\nedge whose two opposite angles sum to more than a half turn becomes the\nother diagonal, when the new facets keep their winding in the parameter\nplane and the new edge passes the split's chord-height limit. No point\nmoves and no boundary edge changes. The worst wall normal is 6.5 degrees\noff; the bar has 642 pickable edges and 0 split pieces.\n\nPinned by feature_edge_g1_join:\nno_pickable_edge_is_a_tangent_piece_of_a_longer_one_in_any_step_fixture\nand tilted_gouge: the_step_bars_wall_facet_normals_follow_the_cylinder.\n\nFixes #2713\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "11d8486eabc8f222e2be13a020d4b1403cf53594",
